---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HubHeader from '../components/HubHeader.astro';
import { path } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Manifesto — AHKH Study Hub" 
  description="The architecture of literature: Transforming raw, monotonous text into enduring knowledge through HTML and CSS."
>
  <HubHeader activeTab="manifesto" />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-reading w-full mx-auto px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <!-- Article Heading Block (Standardized Course Lesson Reader Style) -->
    <div class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-ink-border/80 dark:border-dark-border">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink/80 dark:text-dark-ink/80 mb-2 font-medium">
        <span>Canon 01</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>Foundational Charter</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span class="text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 font-medium">Philosophy</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-4 leading-tight">
        The Architecture of Literature
      </h1>

      <p class="font-serif text-base sm:text-lg text-ink dark:text-dark-ink italic leading-relaxed border-l-2 border-ink dark:border-dark-ink pl-4 py-1">
        "Transforming raw, monotonous text into enduring knowledge through the spatial cadence of HTML and CSS."
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Manifesto Body (Unified Editorial Prose & Component Architecture) -->
    <article id="manifesto-content" class="prose-editorial relative">
      
      <!-- Section I -->
      <section>
        <h2 id="sec-crisis-monotony">1. The Crisis of Monotonous Text</h2>
        <p class="lead text-lg sm:text-xl font-serif text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Knowledge in the digital age is trapped between two hostile extremes. On one side lies the noisy, commercial web—choked by algorithmic feeds, tracking pixels, cookie banners, and aggressive popups designed to fragment human attention. On the other side lies raw, monotonous text: uniform grey paragraphs, dry video transcripts dumped into flat files, rigid scanned PDFs, and academic documentation where every heading looks identical.
        </p>
        <p>
          When text is presented without architectural intention, the mind tires before deep comprehension can even take root. Reading complex systems architecture, cognitive science, or product philosophy should never feel like wading through an undifferentiated database export. Text demands spatial cadence, visual hierarchy, and structural relief.
        </p>

        <!-- Pullout Axiom (Canonical Amber Rail + Wash from Course Lessons) -->
        <blockquote class="my-10 pl-6 border-l-3 border-amber-600 dark:border-amber-500 font-serif italic text-lg sm:text-xl text-ink dark:text-dark-ink leading-relaxed bg-amber-500/5 py-4 pr-4 rounded-r-xs">
          <p>“The medium through which thought is recorded is never inert. Typography, margins, and spatial organization either invite sustained contemplation or enforce mental fatigue.”</p>
          <footer class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-sans not-italic text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300 font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2H20v20H6.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5-2.5Z"/>
              <path d="M6 6h10M6 10h10"/>
            </svg>
            <span>The Sanctuary Canon &mdash; Axiom 01</span>
          </footer>
        </blockquote>
      </section>

      <!-- Section II -->
      <section>
        <h2 id="sec-rearchitecting">2. Re-Architecting with the Power of HTML & CSS</h2>
        <p>
          Our core mission is neither to rewrite original thinkers nor to summarize them away. Our mission is to take raw, unshaped source material and reconstruct its physical vessel. We harness the semantic expressiveness and aesthetic flexibility of modern HTML and CSS to forge literature out of prose:
        </p>

        <!-- Architectural Principles — Canonical Lesson Rail Cards -->
        <div class="my-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose">
          <!-- Rail Card 01: Sky -->
          <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-l-4 border-l-sky-500 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-800 dark:text-sky-300">
                01. Partitions
              </span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="3" rx="2"/>
                <path d="M9 3v18M15 3v18"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-bold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Tactile Containers & Partitions
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink dark:text-dark-ink leading-relaxed">
              Discrete mental units, prerequisite tracks, and module milestones are encapsulated into tactile containers that provide definitive spatial boundaries for the mind.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Rail Card 02: Amber -->
          <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-l-4 border-l-amber-500 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300">
                02. Proclamations
              </span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 21c3 0 7-1 7-8V5c0-1.25-.75-2-2-2H4c-1.25 0-2 .75-2 2v6c0 7 1 8 3 8Z"/>
                <path d="M15 21c3 0 7-1 7-8V5c0-1.25-.75-2-2-2h-4c-1.25 0-2 .75-2 2v6c0 7 1 8 3 8Z"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-bold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Commanding Pullouts & Proclamations
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink dark:text-dark-ink leading-relaxed">
              Seminal principles and foundational aphorisms break free of the body measure, anchored with deliberate weight to serve as conceptual resting posts for contemplation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Rail Card 03: Teal -->
          <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-l-4 border-l-teal-500 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-800 dark:text-teal-300">
                03. Guardrails
              </span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-bold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Dignified Callouts & Ethical Guardrails
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink dark:text-dark-ink leading-relaxed">
              Crucial caveats, contextual footnotes, and ethical guardrails are set apart with dignified framing, illuminating nuances without derailing the primary narrative flow.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Rail Card 04: Purple -->
          <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-l-4 border-l-purple-500 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-purple-800 dark:text-purple-300">
                04. Matrices
              </span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="3" rx="2"/>
                <path d="M3 9h18M3 15h18M9 3v18M15 3v18"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-bold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Responsive Data Matrices
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink dark:text-dark-ink leading-relaxed">
              Dense comparative matrices trapped in static PDFs are liberated into responsive, legible compositions where relationships between variables are immediate, fluid, and clear.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Socratic / Invariant Rule Callout (Emerald rail wash from Course Lessons) -->
        <aside class="my-10 p-5 sm:p-6 border-l-4 border-emerald-600 dark:border-emerald-500 bg-emerald-50/40 dark:bg-emerald-950/20 rounded-r-xs not-prose border-t border-r border-b border-ink-border/60 dark:border-dark-border/60 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 mb-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
              <path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/>
            </svg>
            <span>The Invariant Rule &mdash; Verbatim Fidelity</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-sans font-bold text-base sm:text-lg text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
            We Re-engineer the Vessel; We Never Tamper with the Wine
          </h3>
          <p class="font-serif text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/90 dark:text-dark-ink/90">
            We re-engineer the vessel; we never tamper with the wine. We reject automated AI summaries, unauthorized paraphrasing, and destructive editorial pruning. Every insight, proof, and authorial turn of phrase remains intact. Re-architecture is an act of curatorial reverence, not editorial license.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- Section III -->
      <section>
        <h2 id="sec-editorial-dignity">3. Editorial Dignity, Stability & Visual Stillness</h2>
        <p>
          Great typography requires emotional restraint. In AHKH Study Hub, we enforce a strict visual calm:
        </p>

        <!-- The Invariant Triad — Step Cards -->
        <div class="my-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 not-prose">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-t-3 border-t-ink dark:border-t-dark-ink shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted mb-2">
              <span>Invariant 01</span>
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 12h20M2 12a10 10 0 0 1 10-10M2 12a10 10 0 0 0 10 10"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-semibold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Minimal Motion
            </h4>
            <p class="font-serif text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/85 dark:text-dark-ink/85">
              Zero frivolous bouncing elements, dizzying transitions, or parallax gimmicks. Micro-interactions exist solely to confirm state changes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-t-3 border-t-rose-600 dark:border-t-rose-400 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400 mb-2">
              <span>Invariant 02</span>
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                <line x1="4.93" y1="4.93" x2="19.07" y2="19.07"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-semibold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Absolute Ban on Emojis
            </h4>
            <p class="font-serif text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/85 dark:text-dark-ink/85">
              Scholarly dignity is sustained through classical serif typefaces (<em>Merriweather</em>), crisp sans metrics (<em>Geist</em>), and clean geometric SVG icons.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xs bg-white dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border border-t-3 border-t-blue-600 dark:border-t-blue-400 shadow-2xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 mb-2">
              <span>Invariant 03</span>
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="3" rx="2"/>
                <path d="M7 3v18M17 3v18"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h4 class="font-sans font-semibold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
              Contained Proportions
            </h4>
            <p class="font-serif text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/85 dark:text-dark-ink/85">
              The canvas never expands to swallow high-resolution displays. A disciplined, bookish measure (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-paper-200 dark:bg-dark-border/60 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-2xs text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-semibold">max-w-reading</code> / 68 characters) prevents eye exhaustion and preserves reading endurance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section IV -->
      <section>
        <h2 id="sec-comparative-dialectic">4. The Two Worlds of Digital Reading</h2>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-dark-ink">
          A comparative audit between the commercial web of extractive engagement and the quiet sanctuary of architectural scholarship:
        </p>

        <!-- Comparative Data Matrix Table (Canonical Recipe from Course Lessons) -->
        <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto not-prose">
          <table class="w-full text-left font-serif text-sm border-collapse border-t border-b border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border bg-paper-100 dark:bg-dark-card">
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase font-bold text-ink dark:text-dark-ink">Dimension</th>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase font-bold text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400">Conventional Commercial Web</th>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400">The Sanctuary Standard</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-ink-border/60 dark:divide-dark-border/60">
              <tr class="hover:bg-paper-100/50 dark:hover:bg-dark-card/50 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted whitespace-nowrap">01. Text Rendering</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink/80 dark:text-dark-ink/80 text-xs sm:text-sm">Uniform grey paragraphs, flat raw transcripts, and sterile walls of unshaped text.</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-medium text-xs sm:text-sm bg-emerald-50/20 dark:bg-emerald-950/10">Tactile containers, commanding pullouts, structured matrices, and rhythmic cadence.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-paper-100/50 dark:hover:bg-dark-card/50 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted whitespace-nowrap">02. Data Sovereignty</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink/80 dark:text-dark-ink/80 text-xs sm:text-sm">Notes and annotations locked behind recurring subscriptions and proprietary cloud silos.</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-medium text-xs sm:text-sm bg-emerald-50/20 dark:bg-emerald-950/10">100% Local browser storage with instantaneous, unencumbered CSV and Markdown export.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-paper-100/50 dark:hover:bg-dark-card/50 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted whitespace-nowrap">03. Original Fidelity</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink/80 dark:text-dark-ink/80 text-xs sm:text-sm">Aggressive AI summarization and editorial pruning that flattens nuanced human thought.</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-medium text-xs sm:text-sm bg-emerald-50/20 dark:bg-emerald-950/10">Zero authorial distortion; absolute verbatim fidelity to primary philosophical texts.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-paper-100/50 dark:hover:bg-dark-card/50 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted whitespace-nowrap">04. Reading Atmosphere</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink/80 dark:text-dark-ink/80 text-xs sm:text-sm">Flashing notification badges, bouncing popups, tracking telemetry, and commercial noise.</td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-medium text-xs sm:text-sm bg-emerald-50/20 dark:bg-emerald-950/10">Dignified silence, stable typography, quiet palettes, and undisturbed mental stillness.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section V -->
      <section>
        <h2 id="sec-open-alternative">5. An Open Alternative to Walled Reading Gardens</h2>
        <p>
          Readwise Reader proved that unified digital study is essential for serious learning. But it bound that utility to recurring fees, proprietary databases, and closed ecosystems.
        </p>
        <p>
          AHKH Study Hub stands as a permanent, zero-cost, open sanctuary. Your notes and marginalia are anchored directly to the passages that prompted them, stored securely inside your browser's local memory, and freely exportable at any instant into standard Readwise CSV schemas. No accounts. No subscriptions. Just focused, timeless scholarship.
        </p>

        <!-- Key Principle / Synthesis Card (Canonical Recipe from Course Lessons) -->
        <div class="my-8 p-6 rounded-xs bg-paper-100 dark:bg-dark-card border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border not-prose">
          <div class="text-xs font-sans font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-700 dark:text-indigo-400 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
              <polygon points="16.24 7.76 14.12 14.12 7.76 16.24 9.88 9.88 16.24 7.76"/>
            </svg>
            <span>Key Principle &mdash; Sovereign Knowledge</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-sans font-semibold text-base text-ink dark:text-dark-ink mb-2">
            Permanent, Sovereign, Zero-Cost Scholarship
          </h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/85 dark:text-dark-ink/85">
            Your notes and marginalia are anchored directly to the passages that prompted them, stored securely inside your browser's local memory, and freely exportable at any instant into standard Readwise CSV schemas. No accounts. No subscriptions. Just focused, timeless scholarship.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </article>

    <!-- Floating Highlight Popover for Manifesto -->
    <div 
      id="manifesto-popover" 
      class="hidden fixed z-50 bg-white dark:bg-dark-card text-ink dark:text-dark-ink px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xs shadow-lg shadow-black/5 dark:shadow-black/40 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-ui -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-full mb-2 pointer-events-auto border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border"
    >
      <button 
        id="popover-highlight-btn" 
        class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink hover:text-emerald-700 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 font-medium transition-colors cursor-pointer font-ui"
      >
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="m9 11-6 6v3h3l6-6"/><path d="m22 7-3-3a2.828 2.828 0 0 0-4 0l-10 10 4 4 10-10a2.828 2.828 0 0 0 0-4Z"/>
        </svg>
        <span>Save to Commonplace</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Colophon: Standardized Editorial Attribution & Navigation Footer -->
    <footer class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-ink-border/80 dark:border-dark-border not-prose">
      <div class="p-6 sm:p-7 rounded-xs border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border bg-paper-100/60 dark:bg-dark-card space-y-5 transition-colors">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-ink-border/60 dark:border-dark-border/60 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-ink dark:text-dark-ink shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-bold">
              Canon Specification 01
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted dark:text-dark-muted font-medium">
            Offline-First · 100% Static · Local Storage
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink/90 dark:text-dark-ink/90 leading-relaxed">
          This manifesto is not merely an ideological declaration; it is the living blueprint according to which every lesson, reading track, and marginal note in this hub is engineered. Select any passage above to preserve it in your Commonplace.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center gap-3 pt-1">
          <a 
            href={path('/')} 
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-xs bg-ink dark:bg-dark-ink text-paper-50 dark:text-dark-bg font-ui text-xs font-medium hover:bg-ink/90 dark:hover:bg-dark-ink/90 transition-colors shadow-xs"
          >
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/>
            </svg>
            Return to Index of Curricula
          </a>
          <a 
            href={path('/commonplace')} 
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-xs border border-ink-border dark:border-dark-border bg-white dark:bg-dark-card text-ink dark:text-dark-ink font-ui text-xs font-medium hover:bg-paper-200/60 dark:hover:bg-dark-border/40 transition-colors shadow-2xs"
          >
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"/>
            </svg>
            Review Saved Highlights
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <!-- Client-side Highlight Engine for Manifesto -->
  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      // ClientRouter-safe boot: release the previous page's global listeners first.
      if (window.__ahkhManiAbort) { window.__ahkhManiAbort.abort(); }
      const __ahkhSignal = (window.__ahkhManiAbort = new AbortController()).signal;
      const STORAGE_KEY = 'ahkh_hl_manifesto';
      const popover = document.getElementById('manifesto-popover');
      const highlightBtn = document.getElementById('popover-highlight-btn');
      const content = document.getElementById('manifesto-content');
      let currentSelection = null;

      function loadHighlights() {
        try {
          const items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) || '[]');
          if (!Array.isArray(items) || items.length === 0) return;

          const walker = document.createTreeWalker(content, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);
          const textNodes = [];
          let node;
          while ((node = walker.nextNode())) {
            textNodes.push(node);
          }

          items.forEach(hl => {
            if (!hl.text) return;
            for (let tn of textNodes) {
              const idx = tn.nodeValue.indexOf(hl.text);
              if (idx !== -1 && !tn.parentElement.classList.contains('ahkh-highlight')) {
                const range = document.createRange();
                range.setStart(tn, idx);
                range.setEnd(tn, idx + hl.text.length);
                const span = document.createElement('span');
                span.className = 'ahkh-highlight';
                span.dataset.highlightId = hl.id;
                range.surroundContents(span);
                break;
              }
            }
          });
        } catch (err) {
          console.warn('Could not restore manifesto highlights:', err);
        }
      }

      function handleSelection() {
        const sel = window.getSelection();
        if (!sel || sel.isCollapsed || !content.contains(sel.anchorNode)) {
          popover?.classList.add('hidden');
          currentSelection = null;
          return;
        }

        const text = sel.toString().trim();
        if (text.length < 5) {
          popover?.classList.add('hidden');
          currentSelection = null;
          return;
        }

        const range = sel.getRangeAt(0);
        const rect = range.getBoundingClientRect();
        
        currentSelection = {
          range: range.cloneRange(),
          text: text
        };

        if (popover) {
          popover.style.top = `${window.scrollY + rect.top - 8}px`;
          popover.style.left = `${window.scrollX + rect.left + rect.width / 2}px`;
          popover.classList.remove('hidden');
        }
      }

      document.addEventListener('selectionchange', () => {
        clearTimeout(window._selTimer);
        window._selTimer = setTimeout(handleSelection, 120);
      }, { signal: __ahkhSignal });

      highlightBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!currentSelection) return;
        const hlId = 'hl_' + Date.now();
        
        try {
          const span = document.createElement('span');
          span.className = 'ahkh-highlight';
          span.dataset.highlightId = hlId;
          currentSelection.range.surroundContents(span);

          const items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) || '[]');
          items.push({
            id: hlId,
            text: currentSelection.text,
            lessonId: 'manifesto',
            lessonTitle: 'The Architecture of Literature',
            courseName: 'AHKH Canon',
            url: window.location.pathname,
            createdAt: new Date().toISOString()
          });
          localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(items));

          window.getSelection()?.removeAllRanges();
          popover?.classList.add('hidden');
          if (typeof window.updateGlobalBadge === 'function') {
            window.updateGlobalBadge();
          }
        } catch (err) {
          console.warn('Could not save highlight:', err);
        }
      });

      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        if (popover && !popover.contains(e.target) && !window.getSelection()?.toString()) {
          popover.classList.add('hidden');
        }
      }, { signal: __ahkhSignal });

      // Single boot path: ClientRouter fires astro:page-load on initial load and navigation.
      document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', loadHighlights, { signal: __ahkhSignal });
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
